_refine_special_details
;
 Refined as a 2-component twin.
 Hydrogen atoms were not found in the difference map, so they were not refined
in the structure. The methylammonium positions were found in the difference
map. The carbon and the nitrogen share the same positions in all disordered 
sites. They were refined with EADP and EXYZ. A DFIX command was used to ensure
chemically reasonable bond lengths. Hydrogen atoms were not  included in the
methylammoniums due to the extreme disorder.  SIMU and DELU commands were used
on the aromatic carbons in the 4-fluorophenethylammonium to ensure similar 
behavior.
 The reported SumFormula, MoietyFormula, and molecular weight have been updated
to include the six methylammonium hydrogens.
 The presence of heavy atoms may explain the low precision on the C-C bonds and
the high values resulting from the Hirshfeld rigid-bond test.
 The missing very strong reflections in the FCF may be blocked by the beamstop 
due to the very long a-axis in this structure.
 DISP parameters were generated for this wavelength (18 KeV) using WinGX.
;
